  "description": "With 200 mm of front and rear travel on a rocker link frame, the Boot'r is right at home floating huge airs and drops or pushing through the most technical downhill terrain as fast as possible. Taking feedback from our athletes, such as Greg Watts, we've narrowed the linkage slightly and shortened the chainstays for a more maneuverable, responsive ride.\nTectonic T2 aluminum rocker link DH frame, 12 x 150 mm dropout, replaceable hanger, tapered headtube, and internal cable routing.\nFree Floating Technology™ suspension, RockShox Super Coil Deluxe shock, and RockShox Boxxer 200 mm travel fork.\nShimano Zee 1 x 10 drivetrain with direct mount rear derailleur.\nTektro Slate T4 hydraulic disc brakes and levers, and Schwalbe Magic Mary DH 27.5 x 2.6\" tires on WTB ST Light i35, tubeless compatible double-wall rims.\nThe Boot'r comes in sizes SM, MD, LG. Suggested rider height of SM is 5’2” to 5’6”, MD is 5’5” – 5’10”, LG is 5'9\" – 6'2\".",
